# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository and in every working tree.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (a common Windows default) rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout. That breaks the bilingual build: tools/prepare-i18n.mjs reads the
# working tree and hexo-front-matter matches front matter with a regex that
# expects a bare \n, so every CRLF file loses its front matter and the English
# build silently falls back to the Chinese title, categories and tags.
#
# With eol=lf declared here the working tree matches the repository on Windows,
# macOS and Linux alike.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The theme is tracked as vendored upstream source and gets diffed against the
# upstream release when it is upgraded. Leave its line endings untouched so those
# comparisons stay about real changes only.
themes/** -text

